        fp: "Defendant was in a crowded tavern when a dispute erupted between Defendant and another patron over a spilled beer. The patron shoved Defendant backward against a wall. Defendant drew a switchblade knife from his pocket, opened the blade, and swung it in an arc toward the patron's chest, shouting, 'Back off or I'll gut you!' The patron leaped backward, avoiding the blade by two inches. The switchblade struck an innocent bystander standing next to the patron, slicing through the bystander's coat and inflicting a deep six-inch laceration across the bystander's forearm that severed tendons and caused severe arterial bleeding. The bystander was rushed to the hospital and survived following emergency surgery. Defendant was arrested and charged with battery against the bystander. Defendant argued that he had no intent to strike or touch the bystander.",
